      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Actually, I don't think your two proposed solutions (laser pointer and restoring old menu) would be ideal for resolving this issue. This appears to be an oversight by the developers that should be simply resolved at its source - i.e. preventing left control stick movement from ejecting your character from the chair.\nThe reason I say this is because: \n1. It is understood by players that the way to eject yourself from a chair is by moving your character.\n2. When standing up and having the left-hand Action Menu open, character movement is disabled.\nProvided that we all agree that it's fine for movement to be disabled while the left-hand Action Menu is open, then that behaviour should be extended to chairs as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-10T02:06:37.252Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using the control stick at all pushes your character out of a chair, effectively locking out use of emotes as they've been made exclusive to the radial menu. Allowing the laser pointer to be used on radial menus, or restoring the original Emotes menu (like how Emojis can still be accessed) would fix this as it would no longer require the player to use their control stick.",
